<title>FRANCE: Machinery tops Paris Asian exports in value.</title>
<headline>Machinery tops Paris Asian exports in value.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Machinery, motors, equipment and parts was, in terms of value, the leading category of exports to the Middle East/Asia from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly in 1996, French Ministry of Transport (MoT) figures showed.</p>
<p>The top ten category of goods, in terms of customs  value, expressed in French francs, exported from the Paris airports in 1996, together with 1995 value, in millions of francs were:</p>
<p>					    1996	   1995</p>
<p>    1. Machinery, motors	   13,580	 12,200</p>
<p>equipment &amp; parts</p>
<p>    2. Assorted manufactured	9,970	  9,950</p>
<p>goods</p>
<p>    3. Travel goods/garments/     7,000	  7,600</p>
<p>hosiery/footwear</p>
<p>    4. Perfumes			 3,300	  3,030</p>
<p>    5. Vehicles/transport	   2,050	  1,940</p>
<p>equipment/parts</p>
<p>    6. Medicines/		     1,650	  1,490</p>
<p>pharmaceuticals</p>
<p>    7. Textiles/fabrics		 573	    562</p>
<p>    8. Printed matter		   319	    n.a.</p>
<p>    9. Assorted chemicals	     155.1	  167.8</p>
<p>    10. Dairy products		   81	    n.a.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
